---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How a job works"
  description="How a translation job works, from sending the documents to getting the English files back."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h1>How a job works</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <img
        src="/images/how-it-works.jpg"
        alt="The desk where I translate"
        width="1600"
        height="1055"
        loading="lazy"
        style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:var(--radius);margin-bottom:1.5rem"
      />
      <p>
        <strong>1. You send the documents.</strong> Email me the files and, if you have one, your
        terminology list. Tell me when you need the translation.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>2. You get a fixed price.</strong> I price the job per word and send you the price before
        any work starts. It does not change.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>3. We agree the terminology.</strong> If you have no terminology list, I build one with you
        on the first job and keep it for every later job.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>4. I translate and check.</strong> I translate the documents, then check every part name
        against your terminology list.
      </p>
      <p><strong>5. You get the files back.</strong> In the format you sent them.</p>
      <p>Which documents I translate is on the page <a href="/services/">my services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
